Landed global_config.rs, repo_config.rs, pidlock.rs + tests/settings_pidlock.rs (51 tests) and wired the authorised config.rs seam. On-disk bytes, each pinned against the Node/Bun oracle this run (`node -e 'JSON.stringify(...)'`) and asserted as literals in the test: `<home>/config.json` = `{
  "watch": true,
  "watch_interval": 2000,
  "telemetry": true,
  "daemon": {
    "host": "127.0.0.1",
    "port": 7317
  },
  "budgets": {
    "default_tokens": 1200,
    "max_tokens": 32000
  }
}
` (2-space indent, key order watch/watch_interval/telemetry/daemon/budgets, ONE trailing newline), written through `<path>.<pid>.tmp` + rename and only ever containing the defaults; `<dataDir>/config.json` = `{"watch":true,"watch_interval":2000,"telemetry":true}` (compact, no trailing newline, from write_repo_config); `<home>/daemon.pid` = `{"pid":<int>,"startedAt":"<ISO>"}` compact, no newline, startedAt byte-identical to `new Date().toISOString()` (log.rs's private formatter reproduced in pidlock.rs, pinned by the same 9 Bun fixtures). Clamp band 1000..=300000 (WATCH_INTERVAL_MIN/MAX_MS) with a machine-default fallback for a non-integer/<=0/wrong type; budgets clamp to MAX_BUDGET_TOKENS and default_tokens to max_tokens; port 0..=65535 with 0 honoured; host any non-empty string; repo flags warn per bad-or-missing key (watch, telemetry), global flags warn only on a present-and-wrong key. Single-warning mechanism: an injected sink `pub type Warn<'a> = &'a dyn Fn(&str, &[(&str, Value)])` plus `*_with` variants (the shape registry.rs established), so each test counts the collected lines and asserts exactly one per broken field / per broken file — chosen over spawning a child because log() writes to stderr and a collector makes the count an assertion; no logging dependency added. pidlock liveness: `fs::metadata("/proc/<pid>")`, only ErrorKind::NotFound is dead and every other error (the EPERM analogue, a hidepid mount) counts as alive, commented as the Linux x64 target since libc must not be added; heartbeat is FileTimes set_accessed/set_modified on a write-opened fd (futimens analogue of utimes), no dependency; PID_STALE_AFTER_MS=60_000; acquire = create_new(true) (AlreadyExists is the contention signal), 2 attempts with a real 1_000 ms wait between them (deviation from the TS, which carried RETRY_AFTER_MS only in the error payload — the brief asked for the wait), stale reclaim warns once then unlinks and retries; release refuses an unparsable or foreign pid. config.rs