details.contract:
`migrations.rs` embeds the TypeScript SQL, which is NEVER edited here:
```rust
pub const INIT_SQL: &str = include_str!("../../../../src/shared/store/migrations/0000_init.sql");
pub const FTS_SQL:  &str = include_str!("../../../../src/shared/store/migrations/raw/0001_fts.sql");
pub const MIGRATIONS: [(&str, &str); 2] = [("0000_init", INIT_SQL), ("raw/0001_fts", FTS_SQL)];
pub const LEDGER_TABLE: &str = "schema_migration";
pub const META_SCHEMA_VERSION: &str = "schema_version";
pub const META_REBUILD_REQUIRED: &str = "rebuild_required";
pub fn schema_version() -> i64;                    // == MIGRATIONS.len()
pub fn read_schema_version(conn: &Connection) -> i64;   // meta key, 0 when absent
pub fn read_rebuild_required(conn: &Connection) -> bool;
pub fn migrate(conn: &mut Connection) -> Result<MigrateResult, AppError>;
```
Runner rules, copied from `src/shared/store/migrate.ts` (294 lines): statements split on `--> statement-breakpoint`; one file = one transaction, `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`; ledger row `(name, applied_at)` inserted inside that transaction; only if the ledger lacks the file; a statement failing with `/already exists|duplicate column name/i` is logged and skipped alone; `fromVersion > schema_version()` is `AppError{code:"schema_too_new"}`; a nested transaction is `internal`; `meta.schema_version` is written only by a version change, with the same upsert text.
`schema.rs` holds what a typed model used to provide: the eleven table names as constants, the `meta` key constants (`generation`, `generation_seq`, `project_name`, `project_root`, `project_branch`, `project_remote`, `schema_version`, `rebuild_required`, `indexer_state`, `consecutive_failures`), and a `TABLES: [&str; 11]` list that a test compares against `sqlite_master` after migration — the Rust replacement for `tests/schema-parity.test.ts`.
Tests: migrate an empty file; run twice (second is a no-op); assert `meta.schema_version == 2`; assert the eleven tables plus `node_fts`/`node_fts_state` exist; migrate a COPY of a TypeScript-built graph.db read from `<repoRoot>/.sangkar/graph.db` if it exists, else skip with an explicit message.
